      "target": {
        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix: refresh usage after quota reset boundaries",
        "body": "## Summary\n- refresh usage shortly after known quota reset boundaries when the boundary is earlier than the configured polling cadence\n- suppress repeated prompt retries when provider failures preserve stale data after a boundary refresh attempt\n- cover primary, secondary, and extra rate windows with focused scheduler tests\n\n## Review Follow-up\n- Boundary-triggered refreshes now record the attempted boundary refresh time when the one-shot fires.\n- The scheduler excludes already-attempted boundary refreshes, so preserved stale snapshots fall back to normal polling instead of scheduling another prompt retry.\n- Regression proof: `suppressesRepeatedPromptRefreshAfterAttemptedBoundary` models a preserved stale snapshot after an attempted boundary refresh and verifies no prompt retry is scheduled.\n- No live provider or Keychain probe was run, per repository guidance to avoid live provider probes and keychain-prompting checks.\n\n## Validation\n- `git diff --check`\n- `swift test --filter UsageStoreResetBoundaryRefreshTests`\n- `make check`\n- `swift test --no-parallel --filter '(^CodexBarTests\\.CostUsageScannerBreakdownTests/)'`\n- `/usr/bin/env CODEXBAR_TEST_SUITE_TIMEOUT=420 make test`\n\nNote: default `make test` uses a 180 second per-suite timeout on this machine. The existing `CostUsageScannerBreakdownTests` suite passed but takes about 321-323 seconds locally, so the full suite was run with the repo-supported `CODEXBAR_TEST_SUITE_TIMEOUT=420` override.\n",
